{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 150,
    "dDurationMs": 7180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have a friend named Sammy who back in the\nearly 2000s wrote some code for his MySpace"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "page."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8330,
    "dDurationMs": 4669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what the code did was anybody who visited\nhis page would have his picture and a tag"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12999,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "line that said, “Sammy is my hero,” copied\nover to their homepage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16519,
    "dDurationMs": 3801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that was a bit of fun for a while, but\nSammy wanted more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20320,
    "dDurationMs": 4119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so he tweaked his code so that no only\nthe picture and the tag line were copied over,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24439,
    "dDurationMs": 2311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but also the code itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26750,
    "dDurationMs": 2359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now it exploded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29109,
    "dDurationMs": 3161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In just nine hours he had reached 480 accounts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32270,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 13 hours he was up to 8800."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35540,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in just over 18 hours he had hit a million\naccounts, which was a full 1/35th of all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40650,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accounts on MySpace at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42400,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in a panic, he tried to delete his page."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45220,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when he was successful he actually took\ndown the whole of MySpace with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50560,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was arrested and convicted of computer\nhacking and ordered not to touch a computer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54440,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the next three years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56540,
    "dDurationMs": 6650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I think what this story really tells us\nis just how connected we all are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63190,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine you have 44 friends and each one of\nthose friends has 44 friends who are not also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68690,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your friends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69870,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And each of them has an additional 44 friends,\neach of whom has 44 friends who again has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74940,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "44 friends and they have 44 more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78160,
    "dDurationMs": 6450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then in a chain of just six steps you would\nbe connected to 44 to the sixth or 7.26 billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84610,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people, more than are alive on earth today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88890,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we have contemplated how closely connected\nwe area since long before MySpace even existed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94280,
    "dDurationMs": 6270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Back in 1929 a Hungarian author and poet named\nFrigyes Karinthy wrote a short story called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100550,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101550,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in it, one of the characters challengers\nthe others to find another person on earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105420,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he cannot connect himself to through\nfewer than five intermediaries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109870,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the origin of six degrees of separation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114240,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the theory is correct, it means that you\nwould be connected to the Queen or Tom Cruise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118799,
    "dDurationMs": 1821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in just six steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120620,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they may be the easy ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122420,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What about this shop owner or the Mongolian\nsheep herder?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127020,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the theory really means is that any two\npeople picked at random from anywhere on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130340,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earth would be connected by just six steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133670,
    "dDurationMs": 5510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea remained just fiction until in the\n1960s a Harvard psychologist, Stanley Milgram,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139180,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attempted to test it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140650,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He called it the small world experiment after\nthat phenomenon where you are at a party,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144760,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you meet a stranger and you find out that\nyou have a friend in common and you remark:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148620,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, it is such a small world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150300,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What he did was he sent out 300 packages to\npeople both in Boston and in Nebraska."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157040,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now what he wanted those people to do was\ntry to send their package to a target person"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161340,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Boston, but they weren’t allowed to send\nit directly to him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164620,
    "dDurationMs": 3349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had to send it to someone they knew on\na first name basis who they thought had a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167969,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "better chance of knowing the target and they\ncould forward it on in the same way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172340,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, as you might expect, most of the packages\nnever made it, but 64 did and the average"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177700,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pathway was 5.2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180439,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now six degrees of separation had experimental\nconfirmation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184959,
    "dDurationMs": 1310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or did it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186269,
    "dDurationMs": 5071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look more closely at Milgram’s sample,\nyou will find that of the 300 people, 100"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191340,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were located in Boston, the actual city where\nthe target lived."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195389,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another 100 were stockbrokers, which was the\nsame profession as the target."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199769,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So only 100 people lived in a different state\nand had a different job."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204999,
    "dDurationMs": 5371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of them only 18 of their packages made\nit to the target."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210370,
    "dDurationMs": 5629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we are talking about a sample size of 18\nis all the evidence there was for six degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215999,
    "dDurationMs": 1401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of separation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217400,
    "dDurationMs": 2559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So experimental evidence was tough to come\nby."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219959,
    "dDurationMs": 4521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a decade earlier, a mathematician named\nPaul Erdos had tried to work out the theoretical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224480,
    "dDurationMs": 2019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "properties of networks like these."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226499,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But he didn’t have any information on the\nstructure of real social networks, so he decided"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230930,
    "dDurationMs": 4159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to work on networks where the connections\nbetween nodes were all completely random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235089,
    "dDurationMs": 4441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can actually simulate a network like\nthis using buttons and thread where we just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239530,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "connect up the buttons at random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241139,
    "dDurationMs": 5091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What Erdos found is that when the number of\nlinks per node is small, the network is fragmented."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246230,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pick up any button and few others will come\nwith it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248980,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once you exceed an average of one connection\nper node, the behavior the network changes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253560,
    "dDurationMs": 1149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dramatically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254709,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They almost all link up forming a giant cluster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258340,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you pick up any button almost all of\nthe rest will come with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262150,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This change happens rapidly and it resembles\na phase transition in physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266120,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you could call this a small world network,\nsince the path between any two buttons is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271210,
    "dDurationMs": 1799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "short."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273009,
    "dDurationMs": 4291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thing about random networks is that they\nare naturally small world networks, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277300,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are just as likely to be connected to\nsomeone here in Manila as you are to someone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281610,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in your own town."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283140,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But obviously a random network doesn't represent\nreal life very well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287300,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what do real world networks look like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289990,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for that, we need to go to the empirical\ndata."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292860,
    "dDurationMs": 6010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1994 a couple of college kids invented\na game called six degrees of Kevin Bacon in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298870,
    "dDurationMs": 5139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you try to connect any actor to Kevin\nBacon through just six steps through his costars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304009,
    "dDurationMs": 5141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now a couple of sociology researchers got\naccess to their database of a quarter million"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309150,
    "dDurationMs": 5530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actors and they analyzed the network and what\nthey found was that it was a small world network,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314680,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning between any two actors there were\nonly a very small number of steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319050,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is very similar to a random network."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321340,
    "dDurationMs": 4949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike a random network, the actor network\nalso showed a high degree of clustering, that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326289,
    "dDurationMs": 3241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is, they often worked together in small groups."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329530,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do you get both this grouping behavior,\na high degree of clustering, and the short"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335490,
    "dDurationMs": 2019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "number of steps between any two actors?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337509,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to figure this out they looked at two\ndifferent extremes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341789,
    "dDurationMs": 1741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine a circle of nodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343530,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you connect them at random you get\nthe same outcome as Erdos, short paths between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348860,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any two nodes, but little clustering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351580,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now consider connecting up the nodes only\nwith their nearest two neighbors on each side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356570,
    "dDurationMs": 5719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now clustering is high, but path lengths are\nlong for two nodes picked at random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362289,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if you take this set up and rewire\njust a small number of connections randomly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367789,
    "dDurationMs": 5521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you find is that the path length drops\nrapidly, but clustering still remains high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373310,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the key to modeling real social networks\nis to have a lot of clustering behavior—that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377370,
    "dDurationMs": 6510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is, your friends are also friends with each\nother—but also to have a few random acquaintances."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383880,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the importance of those acquaintances\ncan’t be overstated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386340,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was a researcher named Granovetter in\nthe 1970s who published a paper called “The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391110,
    "dDurationMs": 5399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Strength of Weak Ties,” in which he points\nout: You are much more likely to get a job"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396509,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through those random acquaintances than through\nyour close friends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399909,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you think about it, that makes sense,\nbecause you and your close friends all know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403450,
    "dDurationMs": 2969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same people and have the same information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406419,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is through the random acquaintances that\nyou can get connections with people very far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411139,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from your social circles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412219,
    "dDurationMs": 5191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can find new jobs, new places to live\nand you can be connected to the outside world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417410,
    "dDurationMs": 5559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in fact, it is those random acquaintances\nthat make possible six degrees of separation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422969,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when I want to..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423969,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I am told the degrees have dropped in recent\nyears."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e ...to like four degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Tell me about that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do we know this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429259,
    "dDurationMs": 2831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I don’t know how they measure it, but\nI have tested it and I think it actually has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432090,
    "dDurationMs": 3859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dropped based on how many people have friended\none another on Facebook."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435949,
    "dDurationMs": 3851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The friendship circle has grown, not that\nthey are bosom buddies, but they are people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have access to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442800,
    "dDurationMs": 2639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e And it is... do you know this person who\nthen knows that so that I have access to these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445439,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other people?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446439,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I am told that it has dropped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447439,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As much as the six degrees, we are down to\nfour, at most five."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450979,
    "dDurationMs": 3121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I think Neil DeGrasse Tyson might be right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454100,
    "dDurationMs": 4749,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2011 Facebook analyzed their data and they\nfound that 92 percent of their users were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458849,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "connected through just five steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460979,
    "dDurationMs": 2891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that number is decreasing over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463870,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The concept of six degrees of separation has\nfascinated people for nearly a century."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468860,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think that is not only because of how\ncounter intuitive it is, but also how comforting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473510,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is to know how closely we are all linked,\nnot in some kind of abstract, ill defined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479220,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way, but through hard scientific data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483590,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just six handshakes will connect you to anyone\nelse on the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488360,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I have a challenge for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490160,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the spirit of six degrees of separation\nI want to try an experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494310,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want you to try to get an email to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496439,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you can’t send it directly to me unless\nyou know me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499539,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So assuming you don’t, I want you to send\nit to a friend of yours, someone you know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503099,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a first name basis who you think has a\nbetter chance of getting that email to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507279,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your email eventually gets to me through\na chain of people, I will send you a postcard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511889,
    "dDurationMs": 5511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the mail and I will tally up if we were\nable to get that done in six links or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517400,
    "dDurationMs": 1870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let’s try to do it and see if we can\nconnect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519270,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The instructions are in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524830,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of Veritasium was inspired by\nthe Fine Brothers, Ben and Rafi Fine who are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529270,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "friends of mine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530310,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we are connected through just one degree\nof separation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533620,
    "dDurationMs": 2770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now they have a brand new TV series launching\non TruTV."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536390,
    "dDurationMs": 5170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is called The Six Degrees of Everything\nand it is a fast paced comedic show that tries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541560,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to show us how six things that we don’t\nthink are connected actually are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545170,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It involves sketch comedy and songs and reality\nTV."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548680,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am really looking forward to seeing how\nthey are going to do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551650,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can check it out Tuesdays at 9:30 or\n8:30 central on TruTv."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556160,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am so looking forward to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557480,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And thank you to the Fine Brothers for sponsoring\nthis episode so I could check out the science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561290,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of networks."
    } ]
  } ]
}
